                        GfX by Byteandi (MySTiC /X DESiGN)
         NI (NodeIn) & NO (NodeOut) Written by Spy (MySTiC /X DESiGN)
                 COUNT written by Spy (MySTiC /X DESiGN)



************************ Tools-Description  ***********************************

WHO   - WHO-DOOR also taken as Frontwho
        Features :
                   To the normal informations like username, location, node-
                   number and action comes also now the phonenumber and the
                   number of calls per node. You can also see the filenames
                   per node, if an upload or a download is be made. Depending
                   the userlevel you can show the filenames or not (to be changed
                   in WHO.INFO). If you start up the WHO as a frontdoor the
                   filenames will not be shown (SECURITY ;) )
                   If quietnode is On it`s also not shown to the users. It`s
                   not even shown if they switched on the quiet in the NI-DOOR
                   (see NI-DOOR).
                   Important for Sysops : You can change in WHO.INFO at
                                          starting at which level you can see
                                          the user, even if he did the
                                          quietnode.

NI    - NODEIN-DOOR Shows on the other nodes that a user enters the bbs. You
                    can also allowed certain users in the NI.INFO that this
                    message will not be shown on the other nodes. Then they are
                    going to get a question if they want to be seen or not.
                    If the quietnode was already switched on on this node
                    the question will not be asked.

NO    - NODEOUT-DOOR Shows on the other nodes that a user leaves the bbs.
                     If the quietnode was already switched on on this node
                     it will be automatically shut off by NO, depending if
                     you changed it in the NO.INFO (see NO.INFO)


count - Counts every call on a node. You can start up this tool in the logoff
        script.


************************* Installation description ****************************

After unpacking WHO.LHA there will be 2 directorys : doors/ and bbs/  .
The containing of the directory doors (the dir who/ ) will be copied in the
doors: directory.
In the directory bbs/ will be 2 underdirectories and 2 files :

The directory commands/ :
-------------------------
There are also 2 underdirectories :
bbscmd/ and syscmd/
The containing of the directories comes in certains directories in bbs:commands/
directory.

The directory node-0/ :
-----------------------
In this directory exists 1 file : logoff10.txt
The door NO will be started up at the logoff out of the logoff10.txt. Because
of that the text out of the logoff10.txt must be hang up in front of the still
existing logoff.txt or the file logoff10.txt will be copied in each node
directory

In the directory bbs/ will be 2 files left :
--------------------------------------------
bull10.txt - This file will be hang on in front of an still existing beginning
             bulletin, or if this doesn`t exist it must be copied in the
             directory bbs: . The door NO will be started out of this text.

AddToYourLogoffBatch - The containing of this file must be shown in each
                       logoff batch of each node. In this logoff batch the
                       tool count will be started. It get`s the nodenumber
                       For node 0 would be f.ex. : doors:who/count 0
                       For node 1 would be f.ex. : doors:who/count 1
                       That means, you copy the line out the
                       AddToYourLogoffBatch file in each logoff batch file
                       an changes the node number in case.

That was evereything about the installation



******************** How to change the info files ****************************

WHO.INFO : Following tooltypes are possible : Level_to_see_up/dl
                                              Level_from_sysops
                                              PhoneNumber.Number
                                              Do_not_show_Node.Number

Level_to_see_up/dl : Here you can change the userlevel, where it depends
                     that the user can see the upload or download filename.
                     Level_to_see_up/dl=20 would allowed it starting at
                     security level 20, that the user can see the up- or download
                     filename. If the level is higer than 255, no user (not even
                     the sysop) can see up or download filenames. If the level
                     is 0, each user can see up or download filenames.
                     But : You never see the up or download filenames in the
                           Frontwho, no mattering how low the level is.

Level_from_sysops  : This tooltype shows, beginning when a user can also see
                     users on nodes which are quiet. Level_from_sysops=255
                     would only allowed users with level 255 to see nodes which
                     are quiet. If this number is higer than 255 no user can see
                     a quiet node. If the number is 0 every user can also see
                     nodes which are quiet.

PhoneNumber.Number : This tooltype shows which phonenumber will be shown on a
                     node. PhoneNumber.0=+49 (0)30 745 20 93 would show on
                     Node 0 the phonenumber +49 (0)30 745 20 93.
                     PhoneNumber.1=+49 (0)30 745 20 94 would show on node 1
                     the phonenumber +49 (0)30 745 20 94

Do_not_show_Node.0 : This tooltype gives the possibility (out of the who) that
                     the certain node will not be shown for example with a
                     local node. At Do_not_show_Node.3 the who would not
                     show the 3rd Node.



NI.INFO : Here it gives only 1 possible tooltype :

Name.1=Spy/MST would allow Spy/MST to be not shown to other users. He would
get a question if he wants to be seen from the other nodes.

Name.2=Cindarella/SR the same for a 2nd. user.

here you can enter as much users as you want.



NO.INFO : Also here is only 1 tooltype existing :

Do_not_change_quiet.4 would stop on Node 4 that after the logoff the quietnode
would be deleted. That would be usefull for local nodes, where for example
the quietnode should always be On.

That was everything about the tooltypes.

